        "subtitle": "Combine two arrays with control over the second source.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How the sample directions work",
        "formula": "Combine two arrays with control over the second source.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A tensor is an array with named directions. A sample is one observation; a batch is a group of observations. Each output value adds a value from A to a scaled value from B. Second source multiplier controls that scale; a negative multiplier subtracts.",
          "By default both arrays must have the same shape. Reuse sample directions of size 1 lets a smaller sample repeat across matching directions; this is called broadcasting. Observation groups must still match and never repeat.",
          "The block has two sources. Inspect their shapes and output table in the example, then practice predicting how changing each source affects the combined result. Whole-number arrays support the original equal-shape addition with multiplier 1 only."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open Add example",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/TensorCompositionWorkflowExample.swift",
